  "factCheck": {
    "status": "verified",
    "by": "HeyMariner daily desk",
    "checkedAt": "2026-11-16",
    "notes": "ADMIRALTY (3 Aug 2026): safety depth = (draught + UKC + dynamic factors such as squat, pitch, roll) - height of tide; UKC per company policy; squat based on planned speed; predicted tide may be applied in coastal waters; the 30 m default is not an effective fallback; ENC contours at fixed intervals (2, 5, 10, 20, 30, 50 m) and ECDIS defaults to the next deeper available contour (their example 6.5 m with 5 and 10 m contours displays 10 m). Worked figures 9.8 + 1.0 + 0.6 - 2.4 = 9.0 m are illustrative and arithmetic checked. Pitch/roll allowances and the UKC figure depend on the company SMS; using the lowest predicted tide for the transit window is prudent practice consistent with applying the predicted height of tide for the time of passage."
  },
